Job Description

As a Senior Cinematic Animator at Ubisoft Montreal, you will create high-quality animations for customization content and in-game cinematic sequences for Rainbow Six Siege. Your work will directly enhance the player experience through third-person content such as Victory Dances, loadout poses, and event introductions.

What you’ll do:

• Create animations that align with the visual language and quality standards of Rainbow Six Siege;

• Produce expressive sequences using keyframe animation, motion capture data, and camera work;

• Explore visual approaches and build prototypes to support creative content development;

• Refine animations to ensure strong in-game feel and presentation;

• Collaborate with technical animators, directors, and partner teams to deliver content on schedule;

• Support the evolution of the game’s visual quality by sharing expertise across teams;

• Solve artistic, technical, and production challenges through creative problem-solving;

• Adapt workflows to the realities of a live game production environment;

• Maintain a high level of quality and consistency across delivered content;

• Contribute to cross-discipline collaboration throughout production.

Qualifications

• Experience creating cinematic animation for third-person character content;

• Knowledge of keyframe animation techniques and motion capture workflows;

• Expert with Motion Builder and Maya;

• Understanding of camera work for cinematic sequences;

• Strong attention to visual quality and detail;

• Ability to collaborate effectively with multidisciplinary teams;

• Creative and solution-oriented mindset;

• Adaptability within a live production environment;

• Passion for creating memorable player experiences.

What to send our way

• Your CV highlighting relevant skills and experiences.

• Portfolio or project links adapted to role type.

