Why Join Our Team? 
 Innergex Renewable Energy Inc. is an independent renewable energy producer with an extensive and growing portfolio of assets in Canada, the United States, France and Chile. The Corporation develops, acquires, owns and operates hydroelectric facilities, wind farms, solar farms and energy storage facilities.  

 For more than 30 years, Innergex has believed in a world where abundant renewable energy promotes healthier communities and creates shared prosperity. We are convinced that generating power from renewable sources will lead the way to a better world. We remain committed to responsible growth that balances people, our planet, and prosperity. We believe in offering an engaging, inclusive and supportive work environment where each team member can thrive. 

 Your Contribution! 
 The candidate will play a key role in the preparation of consolidated financial information. They will be able to apply their expertise in consolidation and reporting through various opportunities for process optimization and continuous improvement. They possess an analytical mind, critical thinking skills, and demonstrate sharp professional judgment. 

 Your Day-to-Day! 
 Participate in the quarterly and annual preparation of consolidated financial statements and management reports;  

 Play a key role in the monthly, quarterly, and annual consolidation process for multiple entities spread across various countries and currencies;  

 Prepare analyses and reconciliations for the financial statement line items under your responsibility;  

 Draft quarterly and annual notes to the consolidated financial statements;  

 Participate in the quarterly and annual preparation of financial statements for various entities;  

 Actively participate in various special projects and perform various analyses as needed;  

 Provide support to other departments within the company on accounting matters.  

 Your Skills, Our Requirements! 
 A minimum of 5 to 7 years of experience in a similar role. 
 Bachelor’s degree in accounting 

 Hold a recognized accounting designation (CPA) 

 Experience in a similar position at a major accounting firm (“Big Four”) or a public company with multiple subsidiaries  

 Strong knowledge of IFRS; knowledge of US GAAP is a plus  

 Experience managing multiple currencies is a plus  
 Strong problem-solving and continuous improvement skills  

 Excellent ability to work under pressure and meet tight deadlines in a dynamic environment with shifting priorities  

 Sense of initiative and accountability  
 Excellent analytical skills and attention to detail  
 Strong collaboration and teamwork skills  
 Self-reliance and the ability to learn quickly   
 Bilingualism (French and English, both spoken and written) is required to facilitate ongoing collaboration with various stakeholders outside Quebec. 

 Additional Considerations! 
 The position is based at the company’s headquarters in Longueuil, steps away from the Longueuil-Université de Sherbrooke metro station. 

 This position is at the P3 level. 

