Description
Be Part of a Socially Responsible Organization
Addenda is an investment firm serving both institutional and private wealth clients. We develop innovative, customized investment solutions that support both financial performance and community development.
We manage more than 40 billion dollars in assets and have more than 170 employees spread across our headquarters in Montreal and our offices in Toronto, Guelph, and Regina. We have adopted a hybrid work model that promotes work-life balance as well as a collegiality that sets us apart in the workplace.
The Business Development, Client Partnership and Communication: Where Innovation Meets Client Objectives and Business Growth
Do you want to participate in market growth and development while building client trust through effective communication? You’ll be at the heart of the action, positioning Addenda Capital in a constantly evolving environment. This is a challenge that suits you perfectly.
Reporting to the Executive Vice-President, Business Development and Client Partnerships, your primary responsibility will be to cultivate, develop and strengthen the institutional client market in Canada and globally, to support revenue and sales growth.  You will promote Addenda’s investment solutions to prospective and existing clients while strategically positioning the organization to enhance its market visibility. . In addition, you will collaborate closely with the RFP and Client Experience teams, and other stakeholders to provide high-quality experience to our clients.
Your responsibilities
Develop a yearly and long-term business development plan;
Leverage your business networking skills to attract new business, increase revenue, and meet sales objectives;
Present Addenda Capital’s strengths and communicate our value proposition to prospective clients;
Play a pivotal role in client relations by developing deep relationships with existing clients;
Monitor and analyze market data trends to identify business development opportunities and to connect with new prospects.
Engage team members to improve their performance in terms of quality of service, customer satisfaction, and operational efficiency;
Participate in industry events to maintain an active presence in the business community;
Your profile
Minimum of 15 years of professional experience in a similar role in the investment industry, primarily in institutional market;
A proven track record for developing and executing sales strategies with institutional clients;
Solid understanding of the institutional markets as well as in-depth insight into asset classes;
Extensive investment knowledge of asset classes and the financial markets;
CFA designation and meet the portfolio manager’s registration requirements (compulsory);
Strong knowledge of sustainable investing.
What sets you apart
Influential and interpersonal skills, combined with a customer-oriented approach;
Effective presentation and proposal development skills;
Self-motivated, and results-oriented professional with entrepreneurial drive;
Excellent verbal and written communication skills;
You stand out when interacting with people at different levels in organizations and have a natural ability for forging new relationships;
You are proficient in both English and French, oral and written (English is required to perform daily tasks and interact with clients based in Quebec and other Canadian provinces);
You are available for occasional business travel.
AI utilization
Addenda does not currently use any AI tools or features as part of the recruitment process to select or evaluate candidates.
Status : Permanent, Full-time
Vacancy: 1
Do you have a genuine interest in this position and meet most of the requirements? Apply now! We value differences and discussions by creating and maintaining an inclusive, equitable and accessible work environment that fosters collaboration. Let us know what makes you unique and how you will make a difference in the Addenda Capital team.

Description
Be part of a Socially Responsible Organization
We are a unique asset management firm that stands out for value creation and its pursuit of sustainable wealth for our clients. Thanks to our people's expertise, we can achieve our purpose and participate in the responsible development of our communities.
We manage more than 40 billion dollars in assets and have more than 170 employees spread across our headquarters in Montreal and our offices in Toronto, Guelph, and Regina. We have adopted a hybrid work model that promotes work-life balance as well as a collegiality that sets us apart in the workplace.
The Commercial Mortgages Sector: A Unique Asset Class
Are you interested in joining a team of experts dedicated solely to commercial mortgages, creating long-term value through diversified mortgage portfolios? Addenda Capital is the ideal place to build relationships with key market players and collaborate with colleagues from other sectors.
Reporting to the Team Lead, Commercial Mortgages Administration, you will be part of a team that is responsible to ensure accurate servicing and accounting of mortgage loans. You will champion continuous improvements and challenge processes to ensure business efficiencies and quality client service
Your responsibilities
Ensure accurate loan set up and ongoing loan maintenance based on thorough analysis and understanding of mortgage commitments and contracts;
You manage daily transactions including mortgage disbursements, collections and valuation of mortgage loans;
You review, maintain and enhance department processes on a regular basis;
Promote operational effectiveness by identifying opportunities and proposing innovative solutions for the continuous improvement of processes and procedures.
Work efficiently with key internal and external stakeholders (Servicing Agents, Municipal Tax Authorities, Insurance Agents, Solicitors and Borrowers);
You participate in the upgrade of software, analyze operational impacts, system enhancements and plan and co-ordinate user acceptance testing.
What you bring
A post-secondary education in Business or an equivalent combination of education and work experience;
Minimum of five (5) years relevant experience;
Understanding of the life cycle of a mortgage and end to end servicing operations;
Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite with advanced knowledge in Excel;
Real Estate paralegal experience would be an asset.
What sets you apart
Strong analytical and organizational skills;
Experience with Power BI would be an asset;
A positive client, team and solution orientated attitude;
A high level of attention to detail;
Ability to multitask and prioritize;
Excellent interpersonal and communication skills;
Fluency in French would be considered an asset.
Do you have a genuine interest in this position and meet most of the requirements? Apply now!  We value differences and discussions by creating and maintaining an inclusive, equitable and accessible work environment that fosters collaboration. Let us know what makes you unique and how you will make a difference in the Addenda Capital team.

About the role
The Clinical Research Technician will work with Clinic teams to execute clinical trial activities. Responsibilities of the Clinical Research Technician include execution of tasks performed/clinical activities in compliance with study protocol, Good Clinical Practices (GCP) and Standard Operating Procedures (SOP)s. Please note that this is a variable status position.
What you’ll do here
Ensure the confidentiality of clinical trial participants and sponsors is respected;
Understand protocol driven timed study events and acceptable collection windows (protocol and/or SOP driven) for the timed events;
Report procedural deviations to appropriate supervisory team members;
Preparation and proper clean-up of applicable work-stations (i.e. urine collection station, blood processing station, etc.);
Maintain and advocate a high level of customer service, quality and safety within the department;
Perform clinical trial activities may include but not limited to, sample handling, safety measurements, oral IP administration, and questionnaire administration;
Conduct all clinical trial activities and participant interaction with a high standard of customer service;
Report significant participant misbehavior to Study/Clinical Operations management teams;
Provide feedback, where necessary, to appropriate team members of study progress;
Proactively communicate issues and/or problem resolutions to departmental supervisors and managers;
Complete and/or maintain training as required per jobs needs;
Other tasks as assigned by management.
What you’ll need to succeed
High School Diploma or/and Diploma related to the field of health;
Excellent communication skills in French and English;
Knowledge of another language an asset;
Customer service focused;
Able to work in fast-paced environment.
Altasciences strives to provide a French working environment for its employees in Quebec. Although as part of its francization program has taken all reasonable steps to avoid imposing the above-mentioned requirement. Fluency in English is an essential requirement for the position of Clinical Research Technician including, but not limited to, for the following reasons:
The requirement to have study protocols, designs and clinical research documents written and documented in English as required by industry regulatory agencies.
What we offer
You must be available full-time during the day for the first 6 to 8 weeks of training.
Variable hours.
Day, evening or night shift (no shift rotation).
On site position at our Montreal site (1200 Beaumont);
Accessible by Public Transportation (Metro L'Acadie), Free Parking for employees.
Altasciences’ Incentive Programs Include:
Training & Development Programs
Employee Referral Bonus Program

Company Description
For over 40 years, LGI has built software that healthcare organizations depend on. AI is now at the heart of that work, not as a destination, but as the engine behind our next generation of mission-critical solutions and our enduring mission: helping healthcare organizations perform at their best.
We're looking for exceptional people who are passionate about technology, relentless in their standards, and driven to push what's possible further. At LGI, curiosity isn't a nice-to-have, it's how we work. We're looking for talent who explore and innovate by instinct and want their work to matter beyond the codebase, shaping decisions, enhancing processes, and enabling healthcare practitioners.
Job Description
At LGI Healthcare Solutions, we believe the future of quality assurance lies in combining robust automation with artificial intelligence. We are looking for an experienced software quality professional who wants to help transform our testing practices by leveraging both automation best practices and the emerging capabilities of AI agents. In this strategic role, you will have the opportunity to influence our quality vision, improve the reliability of our Windows and web-based solutions, and contribute to the technological innovation supporting the healthcare network.
Analysis, Strategy, and Testability
Analyze functional, technical, and business requirements to identify risks, ambiguities, and critical scenarios;
Define testing strategies based on risk, business value, and feature complexity;
Collaborate with product and development teams to establish clear and measurable acceptance criteria;
Recommend improvements to enhance solution testability from the design stage onward;
Use artificial intelligence tools to accelerate requirements analysis, propose test scenarios, and improve the quality of analyses while applying critical judgment to the results generated;
Identify automation opportunities from the earliest stages of development.
Automation and Software Quality
Design, develop, maintain, and optimize automated tests;
Contribute to the evolution of automation frameworks;
Integrate automated tests into CI/CD pipelines;
Improve the coverage, stability, and maintainability of automated tests;
Identify the scenarios that offer the greatest return on investment for automation;
Contribute to improving automation best practices;
Help improve software quality by recommending practices that promote stability and maintainability, reduce defects, and increase test coverage.
QA Governance and Transformation
Contribute to the evolution of the team’s quality assurance practices by recommending improvements based on observed results, identified risks, and industry best practices;
Recommend improvements to quality assurance processes, methods, and tools;
Contribute to improving AI-augmented quality assurance practices;
Share expertise and support the professional development of team members.
Artificial Intelligence
Use artificial intelligence solutions to improve the efficiency of quality assurance activities;
Promote the responsible use of artificial intelligence within the team;
Validate results generated by artificial intelligence tools by applying professional judgment;
Identify opportunities to integrate artificial intelligence into quality assurance activities;
Contribute to improving the team’s artificial intelligence practices.
Metrics and Continuous Improvement
Measure and analyze quality metrics such as test coverage, automated test stability, defect density, and validation results;
Use quality metrics to assess the effectiveness of validation strategies, recommend corrective actions, and support the continuous improvement of quality assurance practices;
Contribute to the continuous improvement of validation and automation processes;
Participate in the analysis of quality results to reduce risks and improve delivery performance.
Expected Outcomes
Continuous improvement in automated test coverage;
Reduction in recurring defects;
Optimization of automation practices;
Responsible and effective use of artificial intelligence in quality assurance activities;
Measurable contributions to the evolution of the team’s quality assurance practices;
Improved delivery quality, user experience, and operational performance.
Qualifications
What You Will Bring to LGI Healthcare Solutions to Succeed in This Role:
A bachelor’s degree in computer science or equivalent experience;
A minimum of four to six years of experience in quality assurance and test automation;
Strong knowledge of automation frameworks, CI/CD pipelines, and REST APIs;
Experience designing and executing testing strategies;
Hands-on experience using generative artificial intelligence tools in software development;
The ability to positively influence team practices;
A commitment to professional excellence by keeping your knowledge current, sharing your expertise with team members, and contributing to the continuous improvement of quality assurance practices;
An understanding of the business impact of quality assurance activities and the ability to prioritize initiatives based on risk, business value, and their impact on delivery quality, user satisfaction, and team performance;
The ability to apply critical judgment when analyzing risks, validating results generated by artificial intelligence, and resolving complex problems;
A high degree of autonomy, excellent collaboration skills, and the ability to positively influence your team’s technical decisions;
This position requires bilingualism and an excellent command of French, as you will work with documentation that is primarily in French and communicate, both verbally and in writing, with predominantly French-speaking partners, clients, vendors, and colleagues. A good command of English will be considered an asset.
Additional Information
Why join LGI?
A workplace built on trust, autonomy and collaboration
The opportunity to grow, perform and work alongside curious and talented colleagues
A continuous learning culture with dedicated training time, a renowed skills development platform and access to cutting-edge tools
Stimulating projects that advance healthcare technology and support the work of over 320,000 professionals, benefiting more than 6 million patients
A comprehensive benefits package including group insurance from day one, a group RRSP with employer contributions, 24/7 telemedicine, an employee and family assistance program, and a minimum of 3 weeks vacation per year
At LGI Healthcare Solutions, we value diversity and equal access to employment.

