Company Description
Take your career to new heights at Structube!
STRUCTUBE is the perfect workplace for fans of modern and contemporary interior design, furniture and accessories. We foster an inspiring work environment where collaboration and camaraderie prevail, whether working in our stores or at our Head Office.
What’s in it for you?
A competitive salary;
A group insurance program paid 100% by STRUCTUBE (Vision & Dental);
A telemedicine and stress management program available from day one;
Discounts at various merchants (gym, phone plans, etc.);
A 25% discount on STRUCTUBE’s regular priced items;
Opportunity for growth and career advancement;
An employee recognition program;
And much more!

Job Description
The Marketing Content Creator works on the Marketing Manager’s team and is responsible for participating in the development of Structube’s content strategy, ensuring a coherent brand experience across all communication channels in support of the overall marketing strategy and company objectives. They support the marketing team in the development, execution, rollout, and post-campaign analysis as it relates to marketing communications, ensuring consistency in the brand message and customer experience across all channels.
Ideation, Content Creation & Revision
Production of bilingual (English and French) marketing content, leveraging AI tools to optimize writing, creativity, consistency, and campaign performance;
Content creation for all social media platforms, including but not limited to Instagram, Facebook, Tiktok, YouTube, Pinterest, Linked In, Reddit, X (Twitter);
Review, edit, and proofread marketing content for accuracy, style, and adherence to the brand’s tone of voice;
Research and pitch content ideas and video series, while maintaining Structube’s tone of voice and respecting its brand guidelines;
Research keywords and optimize copywriting for web, respecting industry best practices for SEO and LLM;
Participate in photo and videos shoots related to recommended ideas and concepts (writing scripts, moodboards, storyboards, spokesperson in the video);
Act as brand representative in Strucube’s video content;
Research and stay on top of the latest fashion and design trends and corresponding language, including knowledge of current buzzwords and trending topics to propose relevant content recommendations that align with Structube’s business objectives.
Planning & Coordination
Work closely with the Marketing Manager to assist in planning content themes and marketing communications;
Collaborate with the marketing and creative team to provide content briefs and review of creative assets;
Implement new growth strategies to expand social media and partnership initiatives;
Build and maintain content calendar for all social media platforms;
Coordinate all marketing partnerships ensuring follow-up on all active collaborations to ensure that all partnership conditions are being fulfilled;
Plan all contests and events, ensuring legal compliance and prize fulfillment.
Analysis & Recommendations
Establish per platform objectives, KPIs, as well as growth and retention strategies that align with industry best practices;
Analyze social media data & content analytics to optimize performance and make recommendations for further development and innovation;
Manage report creation for content analytics to measure KPI performance.

Qualifications
Who is the perfect Marketing Content Creator?
2-5 years of experience;
Bachelor’s Degree in Commerce, Marketing, PR, Communications, Business-related qualifications or equivalent experience;
Bilingual: must be fluent in English and French, both spoken and written;
Must be comfortable speaking both English and French on camera as Structube’s brand representative (video and photo);
Strong understanding of social media platforms including: Instagram, Facebook, Pinterest, TikTok, YouTube, LinkedIn, Snapchat, Reddit and X (Twitter);
Creative with strong copywriting skills and knowledge of social media trends;
Attention to detail and ability to multitask while working with tight deadlines;
Self-driven and resourceful with the ability to use one’s own initiative and problem-solving capabilities;
Strong organization, communication, and presentation skills;
Ability to collaborate within a team;
Bonus :
Intermediate competencies with photo, video and content creation;
Experience or interest in artificial intelligence (AI) assisted copywriting, revision, and content creation;
Copywriting experience for B2C retail company;
Experience with influencer marketing;
Experience with business partnerships;
Interest in interior design.

Additional Information
At STRUCTUBE, we believe in equal access to employment and the richness of the diversity of our employees!
About us:
Structube wants to offer its clients a wide range of modern edge home furniture at its best affordable prices! We help our customers rediscover their home, one room at a time. With over 80 stores nationwide and over 700 employees and counting, Structube's small family business has become a thriving retailer brand looking to transform its future retail markets. Join Structube and come experience working with our ambitious, dynamic and motivating team!
Dream a space for them. Dream a career for you!

Overview
Groupe Dynamite Inc. (GDI) is a Montréal-based, public company of integrated omni-channel brands, designing and distributing accessible, trend-forward fashion for women since 1975.
Our mission of "Empowering YOU to be YOU, one outfit at a time" is brought to life through the GARAGE and DYNAMITE banners and represents the consumer-centric core of GDI's long-standing success as a leading retailer in North America.
Today, GDI operates nearly 300 stores across Canada and the United States, as well as shoppable brand experiences at Garageclothing.com and Dynamiteclothing.com.
Job Summary:
We are looking for an SEO Manager to lead all search engine optimization strategy and execution across our GARAGE and DYNAMITE brands—including our transition into Generative and Answer Engine Optimization (GEO/AEO)—growing our digital traffic and revenues, and extending our brands globally, both online and offline. You will manage a team of SEO Specialists and partner with senior stakeholders across IT, UX, Content and E-commerce to turn data-driven insight into results.
Main Responsibilites:
SEO Strategy & Roadmap: Own and evolve the SEO strategy and roadmap to grow North American digital traffic and revenue and support global brand expansion;
AI Search Leadership (GEO/AEO): Lead the brand’s transition from traditional search optimization to Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) and Answer Engine Optimization (AEO)—structuring content, data, and site architecture so it is discoverable and citable by AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity, and other LLM- driven surfaces, as well as building the roadmap, tooling, and team capability needed to make that shift;
Team Leadership: Manage, coach, and develop a team of SEO Specialists/Coordinators—setting priorities, reviewing deliverables, and building the team’s technical and strategic SEO capabilities;
Technical SEO Oversight: Direct ongoing monitoring of the websites and mobile apps to address technical errors and optimize site speed, while leading the digital performance roadmap in close partnership with IT, UX and Digital Product teams;
Keyword & Content Strategy: Guide keyword strategy and online search strategy to deliver optimal ROI against established KPIs, and partner with Marketing and Content teams to embed SEO best practices into content production;
AI Visibility Measurement & Reporting: Define and track AI-search visibility metrics (LLM citations, AI Overview appearances, share of voice in AI-generated answers) alongside traditional organic KPIs, and report on the evolving mix of organic vs. AI-referred traffic to senior leadership;
Competitive Intelligence: Direct ongoing research and reporting on competitors’ SEO, paid search and display strategies, translating findings into actionable recommendations for leadership;
Cross-Functional Leadership: Represent SEO in cross-functional and E-commerce planning, championing new initiatives and influencing prioritization across Marketing, IT, UX, and Content.
Qualifications:
5-7+ years of experience in SEO and digital performance, including 2+ years managing or leading a team;
Expert knowledge of GA4, Google Tag Manager, Google Search Console, Google Business Profile, Bing Webmaster Tools/Editor;
Working knowledge of GEO/AEO and AI-search optimization—structuring and evaluating content for AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity and other LLM-driven surfaces, and tracking AI-referral/citation performance;
Deep technical SEO expertise—robots.txt, metadata, crawl budget and site speed optimization—with the credibility to guide IT/Dev teams on implementation;
Excellent leadership, coaching, and interpersonal skills, with strong written and verbal communication.
Assets:
Experience presenting SEO strategy and results to senior/executive stakeholders;
Strong attention to detail and superior organizational skills;
