JOB DESCRIPTION :
We are seeking a Senior User Experience (UX) Designer for Canadian public sector projects.
RESPONSIBILITIES :
Producing products and services that are user-friendly, and accessible for the endusers;
Participating in all phases of the UX design process, including:
Designing wireframes and prototypes; and
Continuously iterating on solutions.
Designing all the screens a user might interact with and creating the visual and interactive elements that make this interaction possible, such as designing the following features:
Icons;
Buttons;
Menu bars;
Typography; and
colors, etc.
Documenting design specifications by creating annotations for effective hand-off to the
development team;
Contributing to and maintaining the design system;
Creating reusable design components, and optimizing the user interface for
performance;
Ensuring compliance with style guides such as the Canada.ca design system and the
Canada.ca Content Style Guide;
Working in an open, iterative and collaborative way with the CDO;
Working within a strategic context and communicating how activities meet strategic
goals;
Participating in or running design critiques to receive and integrate feedback from
Stakeholders throughout the design process;
QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE :
Post-secondary education mandatory.
More than ten (10) years' experience as a UX Designer.
Experience in artificial intelligence (AI), specifically Claude Code.
Experience in conducting all the following activities:
supporting user research;
creating user personas;
developing prototypes;
performing usability tests;
ensuring compliance with visual brand guidelines;
continuously iterating on solutions with feedback collected through various mechanisms;
complying with accessibility standards.
Demonstrated ability to communicate and collaborate cross-functionally including:
communicating with Project Stakeholders;
collaborating with Agile cross-functional teams;
aligning design with strategic business objectives; and
presenting design work with evidence-based justifications to various Project Stakeholders.
Documentation, insights and presentation of actionable recommendations.
Applying research ethics, data privacy, accessibility, and inclusive lenses to all stages of activities.
Experience working in Agile product team environments.
Spoken and written English required.
Government of Canada security clearance (Reliability) and former public sector work experience an asset.
