  Montréal


What we're looking for

We are looking for a Vice President, Finance and Administration a strategic and detail-oriented senior leader who will ensure Tink's financial health while overseeing the administrative and people functions that support the agency's overall success.

In this cross-functional leadership role, you will oversee two key areas:

Finance and Accounting, financial management, budgeting, financial reporting, tax compliance, and oversight of accounting operations.

Administration, strategic oversight of the Human Resources and Talent Acquisition departments.

As a member of Tink's Executive Leadership Team, you will play a critical role in shaping strategic decisions, ensuring sound business management, and fostering a workplace where people thrive and perform at their best.

Job Tasks and Responsibilities

Oversee all financial and accounting operations of the agency, including client billing, accounts payable, accounts receivable, payroll, bank reconciliations, tax filings, and month-end and year-end closing processes;

Prepare and present monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements to leadership and relevant stakeholders;

Lead the annual budgeting process and closely monitor departmental and project budgets;

Analyze the agency's financial performance, identify trends, variances, and risks, and provide recommendations to leadership;

Ensure Tink's compliance with applicable tax, accounting, and regulatory requirements (GST/QST, payroll deductions, pay equity, etc.);

Manage relationships with external auditors, financial institutions, insurance providers, and legal or tax advisors;

Oversee accounting systems (Dynacom, EmployeurD, or equivalent) and lead their continuous improvement to support the agency's needs;

Monitor cash flow, manage liquidity, and support investment and financing decisions;

Develop and maintain Tink's financial policies, procedures, and internal controls;

Provide strategic oversight of the Human Resources and Talent Acquisition departments, including employee experience, recruitment, HR policies, employee relations, performance management, benefits, recognition programs, and organizational culture;

Act as a strategic partner to leadership on organizational matters such as restructuring, succession planning, total rewards, and change management;

Serve as a member of the Executive Leadership Team and actively contribute to strategic and operational decisions;

Bring financial insight to business discussions, including project profitability, investment decisions, and financial risk management;

Contribute to the development and execution of Tink's business plan in collaboration with the CEO and the other Vice Presidents;

Represent Tink with financial partners, institutions, and government organizations, when required;

Lead, inspire, and develop team members by providing strong leadership, regular feedback, and strategic coaching;

Foster and maintain a divisional culture built on rigor, trust, confidentiality, and continuous improvement;

Oversee performance review cycles across the division and support directors in developing their teams;

Partner with HR leadership to promote organizational health and contribute to the ongoing evolution of Tink's culture.

Required Qualifications and Characteristics

Minimum of 15 years of experience in finance, accounting, and/or administration, including at least 5 years in a senior leadership role overseeing multiple functions;

Strong expertise in financial management, accounting within an agency or professional services environment, and financial reporting;

Proven experience overseeing Human Resources and/or Talent Acquisition functions, with a strong understanding of people management practices;

Good knowledge of Quebec labour legislation and tax regulations;

Strong leadership skills, a high sense of accountability, and the ability to effectively lead across diverse functions (finance, HR, recruitment);

Excellent analytical skills, strong attention to detail, and the ability to clearly communicate complex financial information to leadership and managers;

Proficiency with accounting and management systems (Dynacom, EmployeurD, or equivalent), reporting tools, and the Microsoft Office Suite;

CPA designation and/or a bachelor's or master's degree in business administration, Finance, Accounting, or a related field;

Excellent command of French, both written and spoken; a good working knowledge of English is required for this position

What we offer

Your well-being is at the heart of our priorities. That's why we're proud to offer you the following benefits:

37.5-hour work week with a flexible schedule.

Hybrid work model (2 days per week in person at our office).

Summer schedule.

Paid vacation.

5 paid flexible days off.

Group insurance: medical, dental, short- and long-term disability, as well as travel insurance.

Supplemental health spending account.

Employer contribution to a group RRSP.

Telemedicine service.

Employee Assistance Program (EAP).

A well-established client base and large-scale projects using a variety of modern technologies.

Career growth opportunities.

Reimbursement for training and professional development activities.

Social events and activities.

