SEO Specialist
What’s it like to be a Webtmizer?
Imagine working as an
SEO Specialist
from our super-cool office near Little Italy, alongside a young, diverse team of creative professionals skilled in paid media, SEO, and social media. We are a performance marketing agency founded in 2015, and our team of 20+ experts is growing rapidly.
At Webtmize, our team of creative individuals is our priority, and we ensure to provide them with the best benefits that the industry can offer:
Head to toe Benefits and cheek to cheek,
Working arrangements: Hybrid or in-office;
Continuous learning and development, and opportunities to grow within
Competitive salary and annual salary increases based on performance
Flexible schedules & Working abroad opportunity
Monthly and quarterly Team-building activities
Public transportation reimbursements
Employer Matching retirement plan
On-site parking, including electric vehicle charging stations.
Vacations and much more!
Responsibilities
Generate SEO audits of client websites;
Monitor client websites continually for SEO recommendations, errors, etc.;
Providing recommendations to clients on how to optimize their content for SEO;
Coordinating with clients before and after biweekly SEO meetings to advise them of ongoing SEO action items on our team's side and action items to be completed by them.
Biweekly SEO meetings with clients to advise them of new opportunities to optimize their ranking, alert them of any errors, answer their questions, etc.;
Managing link-building campaigns (includes publisher research, publisher outreach and negotiation, coordinating with clients to advise them of progress and negotiate budget);
Researching/Writing optimized and lengthy content (articles) on various subjects for clients' link-building campaigns.
Requirements
Bachelor's degree in Digital Marketing, Computer Science or other relevant fields;
3+ years of experience in marketing, online advertising and social media;
Strong knowledge of performance marketing, conversion and online customer acquisition;
Intermediate knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite (notably Excel) and Google Analytics;
Knowledge of SEO tools (e.g., Moz, Ahrefs, Screaming Frog) is a vital asset.
Knowledge of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript is a strong asset.
Strong in analyzing data and negotiation tactics;
Strong interpersonal skills with a natural ability to build relationships/connections;
Highly motivated and organized;
Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, performance-driven environment;
Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English and French are an asset.

